--- !u!114 &441980208
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 441980206}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 1f3ef889599182844a2f5643151998e9, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  readingMechanicTutorial: {fileID: 0}
  storyText: {fileID: 163286813}
  fullText: "The Turtle and The Rabbit\n\nOne afternoon, the Turtle and the Rabbit
    met on the road. The Rabbit teased the Turtle about his small feet, saying that
    was why he walked so slowly.\n\nThe Turtle felt insulted by the Rabbit\u2019s
    jokes. Wanting to prove the Rabbit wrong, he challenged him and said,\n\n\u201CIf
    you really want to test my ability, why don\u2019t we settle it with a race?
    You may be fast, but I have strong endurance.\u201D\n\n\u201CWhat kind of race
    do you have in mind?\u201D asked the Rabbit.\n\n\u201CIf you\u2019re willing,
    let\u2019s race to the top of the third mountain,\u201D answered the Turtle.
    \n\nThe Rabbit was delighted by the challenge. He was confident he would win.
    They each invited their friends to watch the competition.\n\nThe next morning,
    many animals gathered to spectate. \n\nThe carabao that had once raced the Turtle
    was there, along with a horse, pig, frog, duck, chicken, dog, cat, goat, cow,
    hawk, deer, wild boar, and others. \n\nEveryone was excited\u2014it was the first
    time they\u2019d witness such a race!\n\nA monkey gave the signal to start.\n\nFrom
    the beginning, the Turtle was left far behind. He moved so slowly that the Rabbit
    could barely see him.\n\nWhen the Rabbit reached the top of the second mountain,
    he still saw no sign of the Turtle behind him.\n\n\u201CAh, I might as well rest.
    The Turtle is still far behind,\u201D the Rabbit said to himself.\n\nHe sat under
    a tree and, exhausted, fell asleep without realizing it.\n\nMeanwhile, the Turtle
    reached the top of the second mountain just before noon. He found the Rabbit
    snoring loudly\u2014likely from exhaustion.\n\nBy late afternoon, the Turtle
    could already see the summit of the third mountain. He was close.\n\nOnly then
    did the Rabbit wake up. He looked down the mountain, assuming the Turtle was
    still trailing\u2014but there was no trace of him. The Rabbit began sprinting
    as fast as he could.\n\nTo his surprise, he found the Turtle already resting
    at the top of the third mountain. The animals cheered and congratulated the Turtle.
    \n\nThe Rabbit felt deeply embarrassed. He apologized to the Turtle for mocking
    him. \n\nFrom that day on, the animals learned a valuable lesson: Never underestimate
    others.\n\n\u2013 THE END \u2013"
  scrollbar: {fileID: 1092530512}
  lineSelector: {fileID: 1092530510}
